# Trivy findings that are not worth acting on.
#
# Each entry is a CVE identifier with an expiry date and a reason. A line
# without an expiry date is permanent, and the workflow hygiene check
# fails the build if one is found — a permanent ignore is a decision that
# has to be revisited, and the date is what forces that.
#
# There are none at the moment. An empty file is the right thing here:
# every finding Trivy reports is a finding worth looking at.
